# Revision applier scope (CPS paper)

Use with **`cps-revision-applier`** only. Applies fixes from an explicit reviewer report or numbered checklist—**does not re-audit**.

## Editable files

- `new/src/paper/overleaf_upload/main.tex` (primary)
- `new/src/paper/main.ltx` (mirror same prose edits)

## May change

- Prose clarity, tense, transitions, bridge sentences (Fig↔Table, pairing).
- Percent **presentation** in text: prefer "4.5\% reduction" over "reduced … −4.5\%" **without** editing `macros_cps.tex` values.
  - May add once in preamble: `\newcommand{\pctmag}[1]{\strip@minus #1}` or rephrase with "by X\%" matching macro magnitude.
- `\figref{}`, `\tabref{}`, `vs.\`, SI/TI/LOS expansions (wording only).
- Section moves **only** when reviewer item explicitly says MOVE and user approved.
- Citations **only** when reviewer gives exact `\cite{key}` and key exists in `references.bib`.

## Must NOT change

- `\CPS…`, `\Abl…`, `\PC…`, `\Lad…`, `\CPSco…` **numeric values** or macro definitions in `tables/*.tex`.
- Equations, propositions, algorithm logic, labels (`\label{}`), `\ref{}` keys.
- Statistical claims, episode counts, p-values, coverage numbers.
- Invent fixes not in the reviewer report.

## Workflow

1. Read reviewer report (IDs or pasted checklist).
2. Apply items in order; skip ambiguous items and list in "blocked".
3. Sync `main.ltx` for every `main.tex` edit.
4. Reply: items applied / skipped / blocked (English, brief).

## Percent fix pattern (abstract example)

```latex
% BAD
reduced ... (\CPSGreedyBWcs\% bitrate ...)

% GOOD
reduced delivered bitrate by 4.5--3.8\% and rebuffering by 9.3--9.2\%
% OR use macro magnitude in prose without duplicate "reduced"+minus
```

Match magnitudes to `macros_cps.tex`; do not round differently.
